# Files and directories excluded from Semgrep's scan. Each entry has a reason
# and was reviewed when added. Adding new entries requires a documented
# rationale; a silent skip is worse than a false positive.

# GitHub Actions workflows use `run: |` with ${{ ... }} interpolation on
# values that are not user-controlled (commit SHAs, workflow refs). The
# `yaml.github-actions.security.run-shell-injection` rule cannot distinguish
# safe interpolation from unsafe, so it fires on every real workflow file.
.github/workflows/

# The local security runner mounts /var/run/docker.sock into Trivy so it can
# scan the images built by this repo. That is the intended way to give Trivy
# access to the Docker daemon without installing it on the host. The
# `dockerfile.security.dockerd-socket-mount` rule flags that pattern, but here
# the alternative (bind-mounting every image tarball) is slower and less
# convenient without improving security.
scripts/security-local.sh

# Token forging is a test-only and demo-only tool. It deliberately constructs
# JWT payloads from attacker-controlled data so the demos can prove the
# verifier rejects tampered tokens. Code-string-concat warnings here are the
# point of the tool, not a bug in it.
scripts/forge-token.ts
